#: ../../source/community/licencing.md:1
msgid "版权"
msgstr "Copyright"

#: ../../source/community/licencing.md:4 ../../source/community/licencing.md:8
msgid "一张图读懂灵数奇缘社区资产授权规则"
msgstr ""
"Understanding the Luv Sense Digital Community Asset Licensing Rules at a "
"Glance"

#: ../../source/community/licencing.md:11
msgid "Q&A"
msgstr "Q&A"

#: ../../source/community/licencing.md:13
msgid "**为什么任何人都可以访问和下载社区资产，社区资产不需要做保护吗？**"
msgstr ""
"**Why can anyone access and download community assets? Don't community "
"assets need protection?**"

#: ../../source/community/licencing.md:15
msgid "&emsp;&emsp;有两个原因，一是如果无法访问社区资产，任何人也没法基于已有社区资产做出自己的首次创作和贡献。也就是说，我们认为任何有兴趣加入社区的人的先决条件必须是先能接触社区资产，才有深入参与互动的可能。二是下载文件不代表已经“拥有”，要获得私自创作发布的授权还得为社区做出能被接纳的任意贡献。另外关于数字资产文件本身的严格保护和访问控制，在互联网上基本没可能实现，各种倒卖素材和私下分享也是常见现象。我们认为目前更加有效的数字版权的保护和流转可以通过区块链技术和NFT。"
msgstr ""
"&emsp;&emsp;There are two reasons. First, if community assets cannot be "
"accessed, no one would be able to make their first creative contribution "
"based on existing community assets. In other words, we believe that a "
"prerequisite for anyone interested in joining the community is the "
"ability to access community assets first, which makes deeper "
"participation and interaction possible. Second, downloading files does "
"not mean \"owning\" them. To obtain authorization for private creative "
"publishing, one must still make an acceptable contribution to the "
"community. Additionally, strict protection and access control of digital "
"asset files themselves are essentially impossible to achieve on the "
"internet, with various resale of materials and private sharing being "
"common phenomena. We believe that more effective digital copyright "
"protection and transfer can be achieved through blockchain technology and"
" NFTs."

#: ../../source/community/licencing.md:17
msgid "**什么样的社区贡献可以被采纳？**"
msgstr "**What kind of community contributions can be accepted?**"

#: ../../source/community/licencing.md:19
msgid ""
"&emsp;&emsp;简单说是不违背法律法规的任何内容。其中包括不接纳侵犯他人版权的内容，不接纳容易带来负面影响争议的敏感内容，以及创作质量过低的提交物。其它只要是有效质量的内容，不论内容量多少都愿意采纳（只贡献一行有价值的程序代码、文案也符合采纳要求）。首次得到采纳就意味着你成为了社区伙伴的一员，就可以获得所有社区资产的商用授权了。另外，如果是贡献的是资金捐赠的话，那就不用谈条件采纳了，关于捐赠金额的要求的话，当然是"
" <del>越多越好</del> 任意金额即可。"
msgstr ""
"&emsp;&emsp;Simply put, any content that does not violate laws and "
"regulations. This includes not accepting content that infringes on "
"others' copyrights, not accepting sensitive content that could easily "
"cause negative controversy, and not accepting submissions with overly low"
" creative quality. Any other content of reasonable quality, regardless of"
" the amount, is welcome to be accepted (even contributing a single line "
"of valuable code or writing meets the acceptance criteria). Being "
"accepted for the first time means you become a member of the community "
"partners and can obtain commercial licensing for all community assets. "
"Additionally, if the contribution is a financial donation, there are no "
"conditions for acceptance — regarding the donation amount, of course it's"
"  <del>the more the better</del> any amount is fine."

#: ../../source/community/licencing.md:21
msgid "**可以解释一下Level 1的授权是怎么回事吗？**"
msgstr "**Can you explain what Level 1 licensing is about?**"

#: ../../source/community/licencing.md:23
msgid ""
"&emsp;&emsp;简单一点解释，就是首次被采纳社区贡献后就能获得对社区资产相当于[CC BY "
"4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/deed.zh)的授权，只用保留和展示对《灵数奇缘》社区的署名（名字、网站链接等），就可以做修改、转换、再创作和发布商业作品。但是有部分社区资产存在更宽泛的授权协议，比如开源的Dora"
" SSR游戏引擎、Yuescript编程语言以及Game 0游戏工程下的程序代码都是MIT开源授权。获取和使用这些程序代码并不需要成为社区成员。"
msgstr ""
"&emsp;&emsp;To put it simply, after your first community contribution is "
"accepted, you receive licensing equivalent to [CC BY "
"4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/deed.en) for community "
"assets. You only need to retain and display attribution to the Luv Sense "
"Digital community (name, website link, etc.), and you can modify, "
"transform, recreate, and publish commercial works. However, some "
"community assets have broader licensing agreements, such as the open-"
"source Dora SSR game engine, the Yuescript programming language, and the "
"program code under the Game 0 project, all of which are under the MIT "
"open-source license. Accessing and using these program codes does not "
"require becoming a community member."

#: ../../source/community/licencing.md:25
msgid "**参与社区DAO建设是要做些什么？**"
msgstr "**What does participating in community DAO building involve?**"

#: ../../source/community/licencing.md:27
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"&emsp;&emsp;建立DAO运营模式的组织是一个需要长期实践探索的工作。DAO（Decentralized Autonomous "
"Organization，去中心化自组织机构，中文环境有人叫作“岛”，个人认为不如叫作“道”）建立有三个基础条件：   "
"&emsp;&emsp;**1、目标共享**   &emsp;&emsp;具有能与陌生人达成共识的组织目标和组织文化（组织的使命、愿景、价值观）。"
"   &emsp;&emsp;**2、制度共建**   "
"&emsp;&emsp;具有能与陌生人达成共识的包含创立、治理、激励等内容的规则体系，且此规则通过区块链技术置于链上。   "
"&emsp;&emsp;**3、利益共有**   &emsp;&emsp;具有能与所有参与者形成利益关联的Token来实现全员激励。   "
"&emsp;&emsp;乍一看传统组织似乎也同样在做这些行为，但是DAO的核心区别在于通过区块链技术实现让组织内的信息流动公开和透明化。传统组织做分层管理，在工作群体间建立信息差，从而使少数决策者容易实现分而治之的效果，并以个人意志左右组织活动。DAO通过区块链，共享决策所需信息，按约定的制度计量成员付出的劳动，采用取得共识的多种更优的投票方式，衡量效率和公正度，最终达成群体共同参与的决策。二者组织的思路是完全不同的，也和传统中大家工作生活的认知体验完全不同，需要长期的学习和实践才能真正走出这条“道”。"
msgstr ""
"&emsp;&emsp;Building an organization with a DAO operating model is work "
"that requires long-term practice and exploration. A DAO (Decentralized "
"Autonomous Organization) has three foundational requirements for "
"establishment:   &emsp;&emsp;**1. Shared Goals**   &emsp;&emsp;Having "
"organizational goals and culture (mission, vision, values) that can reach"
" consensus with strangers.   &emsp;&emsp;**2. Co-built Institutions**   "
"&emsp;&emsp;Having a rule system including creation, governance, and "
"incentives that can reach consensus with strangers, with these rules "
"placed on-chain through blockchain technology.   &emsp;&emsp;**3. Shared "
"Interests**   &emsp;&emsp;Having Tokens that form interest associations "
"with all participants to achieve full-member incentives.   &emsp;&emsp;At"
" first glance, traditional organizations seem to do the same things, but "
"the core difference of DAOs lies in using blockchain technology to make "
"information flow within the organization public and transparent. "
"Traditional organizations use hierarchical management, creating "
"information asymmetry between work groups, making it easy for a few "
"decision-makers to achieve divide-and-conquer effects and influence "
"organizational activities with personal will. DAOs use blockchain to "
"share information needed for decision-making, measure members' labor "
"contributions according to agreed-upon systems, adopt multiple consensual"
" and superior voting methods, weigh efficiency and fairness, and "
"ultimately achieve group-participatory decisions. The organizational "
"thinking of the two is fundamentally different, and also quite different "
"from everyone's traditional work and life experience, requiring long-term"
" learning and practice to truly walk this \"path\"."

#: ../../source/community/licencing.md:36
msgid "**最后问一下提到NFT，和比特币一样是一种金融诈骗的工具吗？**"
msgstr ""
"**Finally, regarding NFTs — are they a financial fraud tool like "
"Bitcoin?**"

#: ../../source/community/licencing.md:38
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"&emsp;&emsp;是的。NFT和加密货币是一种天生具有金融属性的工具。随着现有运行制度、规则和监管的不完善，目前是很容易被人用作设立骗局和进行诈骗的工具。为了防止陷入这样的骗局，需要多加警惕各种圈的“玩法”（大多都是伪装成游戏形式的赌局）。"
"   &emsp;&emsp;现状既然是这样，《灵数奇缘》社区为什么还要涉足NFT呢？因为NFT（Non-Fungible "
"Token）的本质是一种数字的所有权凭证。作为它原初的意义，在声明数字版权的领域是有存在价值的。就像我们前面讨论的，一件数字作品的文件被复制传播了，是不是所有权就丢失了的问题。有区块链和NFT以后，这个问题才有了更好的解答。这个也是为我们《灵数奇缘》社区创作者能保存和流通自己有价值的创作品，希望探索的新的方法。"
msgstr ""
"&emsp;&emsp;Yes. NFTs and cryptocurrencies are inherently financial "
"instruments. With current operating systems, rules, and regulations being"
" imperfect, they can easily be used as tools for setting up scams and "
"fraud. To avoid falling into such scams, one needs to be vigilant about "
"various \"gameplay\" in different circles (most of which are gambling "
"disguised as games).   &emsp;&emsp;Given this situation, why does the Luv"
" Sense Digital community still venture into NFTs? Because the essence of "
"NFTs (Non-Fungible Tokens) is a digital proof of ownership. In their "
"original sense, they have value in the field of declaring digital "
"copyrights. As we discussed earlier, there's the question of whether a "
"digital work's ownership is lost once its file is copied and distributed."
" With blockchain and NFTs, this question has a better answer. This is "
"also a new method we hope to explore for Luv Sense Digital community "
"creators to preserve and circulate their valuable creative works."

